  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    user_intent: "Model Upgrade and Configuration\nThe user wants to upgrade the AI model to the latest \"Nano Banana 2\" (which is interpreted as Gemini 3 Pro) and configure it for high-quality image generation, including 4K resolution. They also want to integrate model selection (Flash vs. Pro) and image size options into the application\'s UI and functionality."
    session_summary: "The user wants to change the current Gemini 3 Pro model to the latest \"Nano Banana 2\".\n\nBased on the provided file contents and the conversation, here\'s a summary of the work done and the context for future steps:\n\n**User Goals:**\n\n*   Switch the current Gemini 3 Pro model to \"Nano Banana 2\".\n*   Understand the implications of using different Gemini models (Flash vs. Pro) for image generation, specifically regarding quality and speed.\n*   Potentially upgrade to 4K image generation.\n\n**Key Information and Context:**\n\n*   **Application Structure:** The application uses React and is built with Vite. It leverages `@google/genai` for AI functionalities.\n*   **Gemini Models:**\n    *   The application currently supports `gemini-2.5-flash-image` (for speed and free usage) and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` (for higher quality, requiring a paid API key).\n    *   The user\'s request for \"Nano Banana 2\" seems to be a misunderstanding or a colloquial name for a Gemini 3 model. The available Gemini 3 models in the codebase are `gemini-3-flash-preview` and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview`.\n    *   The `App.tsx` file contains logic to switch between `generationModel` states (\'flash\' and \'pro\').\n*   **Image Generation Capabilities:**\n    *   `gemini-2.5-flash-image` is used for faster, free image generation, typically producing 1K images.\n    *   `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` is available for higher quality images and supports specifying `imageSize` (e.g., \'4K\'). This model requires a paid API key.\n*   **Codebase Modifications:**\n    *   The `App.tsx` file has been modified to include:\n        *   State variables `generationModel` and `imageSize`.\n        *   UI elements in the sidebar to select between \'flash\' and \'pro\' models.\n        *   Conditional display of `imageSize` options when \'pro\' is selected.\n        *   The `handleGenerate` function has been updated to:\n            *   Check for API key availability (`window.aistudio.hasSelectedApiKey()`) and prompt for selection (`window.aistudio.openSelectKey()`) when the \'pro\' model is chosen.\n            *   Use `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` and pass the `imageSize` parameter when \'pro\' is selected.\n            *   Use `gemini-2.5-flash-image` for the \'flash\' model.\n        *   Translations for new UI elements related to model selection and image size have been added.\n    *   The `metadata.json` file has been updated to reflect the Gemini 3 Flash upgrade.\n*   **Dependencies:** `@google/genai`, `react`, `react-dom`, and related development dependencies are installed.\n*   **Environment Variables:** `process.env.API_KEY` is used for the Google GenAI API key. The application relies on `window.aistudio` for managing API key selection, which is assumed to be available in the execution environment.\n*   **User Preferences:**\n    *   The user wants to use the latest models.\n    *   The user is interested in higher resolution image generation (4K).\n    *   The user needs to understand the trade-offs (speed, cost) between different models.\n\n**Current Blockers/Issues:**\n\n*   The user\'s request for \"Nano Banana 2\" needs clarification, as the codebase uses standard Gemini model names. The assumption is they mean a Gemini 3 model.\n*   The `getAi` function in `App.tsx` was refactored to use `ai.current` for memoization, but the `handleGenerate` function was updated to re-instantiate `GoogleGenAI` to ensure the latest API key is used. This might need further review for consistency.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n\n1.  **Clarify \"Nano Banana 2\":** Confirm with the user if they are referring to `gemini-3-flash-preview` or `gemini-3-pro-image-preview`. Based on the context, it\'s likely they want the best available model, which would be `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` for quality.\n2.  **Implement 4K Generation:** If the user confirms they want to use `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` for higher quality and potentially 4K generation, ensure the `imageSize` is correctly set to \'4K\' in the `handleGenerate` function when the \'pro\' model is selected.\n3.  **Review API Key Handling:** Ensure the API key selection and instantiation logic in `handleGenerate` is robust and handles cases where `window.aistudio` might not be available or when the user cancels the API key selection.\n4.  **Finalize UI Integration:** Ensure the `InfiniteCanvas` component correctly displays and handles the `imageSize` dropdown based on the `generationModel` state.\n5.  **Testing:** Thoroughly test image generation with both \'flash\' and \'pro\' models, and with different `imageSize` settings, to verify functionality and identify any performance issues.\n\nThis summary provides a detailed overview of the project\'s state, the implemented features, and the path forward to address the user\'s request."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>348;747-753;755-761;763-769;771-777;779-785;787-793;795-801;803-809;811-817;819-825;827-833;835-841;843-849;851-857;859-865;867-873;875-881;883-889;891-897;899-905;907-913;915-921;923-929;931-937;939-945;947-953;955-961;963-969;971-977;979-985;987-993;995-1001;1003-1009;1011-1017;1019-1025;1027-1033;1035-1041;1043-1049;1051-1057;1059-1065;1067-1073;1075-1081;1083-1089;1091-1097;1099-1105;1107-1113;1115-1121;1123-1129;1131-1137;1139-1145;1147-1153;1155-1161;1163-1169;1171-1177;1179-1185;1187-1193;1195-1201;1203-1209;1211-1217;1219-1225;1227-1233;1235-1241;1243-1249;1251-1257;1259-1265;1267-1273;1275-1281;1283-1289;1291-1297;1299-1305;1307-1313;1315-1321;1323-1329;1331-1337;1339-1345;1347-1353;1355-1361;1363-1369;1371-1377;1379-1385;1387-1393;1395-1401;1403-1409;1411-1417;1419-1425;1427-1433;1435-1441;1443-1449;1451-1457;1459-1465;1467-1473;1475-1481;1483-1489;1491-1497;1499-1505;1507-1513;1515-1521;1523-1529;1531-1537;1539-1545;1547-1553;1555-1561;1563-1569;1571-1577;1579-1585;1587-1593;1595-1601;1603-1609;1611-1617;1619-1625;1627-1633;1635-1641;1643-1649;1651-1657;1659-1665;1667-1673;1675-1681;1683-1689;1691-1697;1699-1705;1707-1713;1715-1721;1723-1729;1731-1737;1739-1745;1747-1753;1755-1761;1763-1769;1771-1777;1779-1785;1787-1793;1795-1801;1803-1809;1811-1817;1819-1825;1827-1833;1835-1841;1843-1849;1851-1857;1859-1865;1867-1873;1875-1881;1883-1889;1891-1897;1899-1905;1907-1913;1915-1921;1923-1929;1931-1937;1939-1945;1947-1953;1955-1961;1963-1969;1971-1977;1979-1985;1987-1993;1995-2001;2003-2009;2011-2017;2019-2025;2027-2033;2035-2041;2043-2049;2051-2057;2059-2065;2067-2073;2075-2081;2083-2089;2091-2097;2099-2105;2107-2113;2115-2121</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Modified the `handleGenerate` function to conditionally use `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` for \'pro\' generation model. This includes checking for API key availability, instantiating `GoogleGenAI` with the correct key, and setting `imageConfig` with `imageSize`. Also updated the `generationModel` state initialization and added corresponding translations.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/vite.config.ts</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>13-17</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` to the `define` object to make the API key available in the client-side code.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-2123</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file contains the main application logic. It handles state management for canvas elements, user interactions, and AI model integration. Key functions related to image generation (`handleGenerate`) and AI model selection (`generationModel`, `imageSize`) were identified as relevant to the user\'s request.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/vite.config.ts</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-23</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file configures Vite, the build tool. It defines server settings and plugins. Crucially, it shows how environment variables like `GEMINI_API_KEY` are loaded and made available to the client-side code via the `define` option, which is essential for using the Google GenAI SDK.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:handleGenerate</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This function is responsible for generating images. It contains logic for selecting the AI model (`generationModel`), checking for API key availability, and configuring image generation parameters like `imageSize`. This is the primary function that needs modification to support the user\'s request for Gemini 3 Pro and higher resolutions.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:generationModel</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This state variable in `App.tsx` controls which AI model is used for image generation (\'flash\' or \'pro\'). It\'s directly linked to the user\'s request to switch to Gemini 3 Pro.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:imageSize</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This state variable in `App.tsx` controls the desired output size for generated images (e.g., \'1K\', \'2K\', \'4K\'). It\'s crucial for fulfilling the user\'s request for higher resolution images.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>vite.config.ts:define</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This section in `vite.config.ts` exposes environment variables to the client-side code. Specifically, `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` is made available, which is necessary for the `GoogleGenAI` SDK to use the provided API key.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:usingPro</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This is a translation key used in `App.tsx` to display information to the user about using the Pro model, including the requirement for a paid API key. This was updated to reflect the change to Gemini 3 Pro.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:qualityPro</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This is a translation key used in `App.tsx` to label the \"Quality (Pro)\" option for model selection. This was updated to reflect the change to Gemini 3 Pro.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:usingFlash</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This is a translation key used in `App.tsx` to display information about using the Flash model. It was updated to specify Gemini 2.5 Flash for clarity, as the user\'s request focused on upgrading the *Pro* model, not necessarily replacing the Flash model for all use cases.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:speedFlash</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This is a translation key used in `App.tsx` to label the \"Speed (Flash)\" option for model selection. This was updated to specify Gemini 2.5 Flash for clarity.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>"
