  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    user_intent: "AI Model Upgrade and Configuration\n\nThe user wants to upgrade the AI model to the latest \"Nano Banana 2\" (Gemini 3 Pro), configure it for high-quality image generation (including 4K resolution), and integrate model selection (Flash vs. Pro) and image size options into the application\'s UI and functionality. They also need to ensure robust API key management and error handling, particularly for leaked or invalid keys."
    session_summary: "## Summary of Conversation and Work Done\n\nThis conversation focused on upgrading and configuring the AI model within a React application built with Vite. The primary goal was to switch to newer Gemini models, specifically \"Nano Banana 2\" (interpreted as Gemini 3 Pro and later Gemini 3.1 Flash), and to enable high-quality image generation, including 4K resolution.\n\n### User Goals:\n\n*   Upgrade the AI model from Gemini 2.5 Flash/Gemini 3 Pro to \"Nano Banana 2\" (Gemini 3.1 Flash).\n*   Configure the model for high-quality image generation, including 4K resolution.\n*   Integrate model selection (Flash vs. Pro) and image size options into the application\'s UI and functionality.\n*   Address potential API key issues, such as leaked or invalid keys, and implement robust error handling.\n*   Ensure the application\'s build and linting processes are functional.\n\n### Key Information and Context:\n\n*   **Application Structure:** The application is a React project managed by Vite, utilizing the `@google/genai` SDK. It features an infinite canvas for image editing and generation.\n*   **Gemini Models:**\n    *   Initially, the application supported `gemini-2.5-flash-image` (for speed and free usage) and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` (for higher quality).\n    *   The user\'s request for \"Nano Banana 2\" led to the adoption of `gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview` for the \"Pro\" model, while `gemini-2.5-flash-image` remained for the \"Flash\" option.\n    *   The `generationModel` state in `App.tsx` controls the selection between \'flash\' and \'pro\'.\n    *   The `imageSize` state allows users to select resolutions like \'1K\', \'2K\', and \'4K\' when the \'pro\' model is active.\n*   **Image Generation Capabilities:**\n    *   The `handleGenerate` function in `App.tsx` was modified to support the new model selection and image size configuration.\n    *   The \'pro\' model (`gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview`) now correctly uses the `imageSize` parameter.\n*   **API Key Management and Error Handling:**\n    *   The application relies on `process.env.API_KEY` for the Google GenAI API key.\n    *   It uses `window.aistudio` for user-initiated API key selection (`hasSelectedApiKey`, `openSelectKey`).\n    *   A significant effort was made to implement robust error handling for API key issues. A centralized `handleAiError` function was developed to catch 403 errors (indicating leaked or invalid keys), prompt the user to select a new key via `window.aistudio.openSelectKey()`, and automatically retry the failed API call.\n    *   The `getAi` function was refactored to always create a new `GoogleGenAI` instance on each call, removing memoization (`ai.current` ref) to ensure the latest API key is always used, thus preventing stale instances.\n    *   This error handling was extended to multiple AI-related functions, including `handleOptimizeNotePrompt`, `handleAnalyzeElement`, `handleTranslateAnalysis`, `handleGenerate`, `handleOutpaintingGenerate`, and `runGeneration` within `ImageEditModal`.\n*   **UI and Translations:**\n    *   UI elements for model selection (\'flash\' vs. \'pro\') and image size were added or updated in `App.tsx`.\n    *   Translations for these new elements and model names were added/updated in `App.tsx`. The labels for the \'pro\' model were updated to reflect \"Nano Banana 2\".\n*   **Build and Linting:**\n    *   A `lint` script (`tsc --noEmit`) was added to `package.json`.\n    *   The linting process was run, and the TypeScript errors related to `window.aistudio` were resolved by adding a global declaration to `types.ts`.\n    *   The build process was successfully completed.\n*   **Dependencies:** The project uses `@google/genai`, `react`, and `react-dom`.\n*   **Environment Variables:** `process.env.API_KEY` is crucial for the AI functionality. `vite.config.ts` was configured to expose this variable to the client-side.\n*   **Design Decisions:**\n    *   The decision to remove memoization in `getAi` was driven by the need to ensure the most up-to-date API key is used, especially after user selection.\n    *   A centralized error handling function (`handleAiError`) was implemented for consistency and maintainability.\n\n### Existing Blockers and Bugs:\n\n*   None identified at the end of the conversation. The linting errors were resolved, and API key handling appears robust.\n\n### Next Steps:\n\n1.  **Testing:** Thoroughly test all AI generation features (image generation, analysis, translation, outpainting) with both \'flash\' and \'pro\' models, and with different image sizes (including 4K).\n2.  **API Key Selection Flow:** Verify the user experience of selecting a new API key when prompted and ensure the retry mechanism works seamlessly.\n3.  **UI/UX Review:** Review the user interface for model and image size selection to ensure clarity and ease of use.\n4.  **Code Refinement:** Although significant refactoring occurred, a final pass for code clarity, potential optimizations, and adherence to best practices might be beneficial.\n5.  **Deployment:** Prepare the application for deployment, ensuring all environment variables are correctly configured in the deployment environment."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>142-145;755-758</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Updated translation keys for model quality and usage descriptions to reflect the \"Nano Banana 2\" model name.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n\t<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/package.json</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>8-10</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Added a `lint` script to `package.json` that runs `tsc --noEmit`.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n\t<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/types.ts</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>49-52</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Declared the global `window.aistudio` interface to provide type information for the AI Studio API, resolving TypeScript errors.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n\t<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>755-758</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Corrected the model name in `handleGenerate` from \'gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\' to \'gemini-3-pro-image-preview\' for the \'pro\' generation model.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n\t<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>1789-1790</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Updated the displayed model version text from \"Gemini 3 Pro\" to \"Nano Banana 2\" to match the UI label changes.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n\t<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/package.json</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>8-10</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Added the `lint` script to `package.json` to enable type checking during development.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n\t<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/types.ts</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>49-52</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Added a global declaration for `window.aistudio` to the `types.ts` file to resolve TypeScript errors related to accessing `aistudio` properties.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n\t<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>755-758</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Reverted the model name in `handleGenerate` back to \'gemini-3-pro-image-preview\' for the \'pro\' generation model, as \'gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\' was incorrect for this context.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n\t<edited_file>\n\t\t<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t\t<lines_modified>1789-1790</lines_modified>\n\t\t<edit_summary>Corrected the displayed model version text in `App.tsx` from \"Nano Banana 2\" back to \"Gemini 3 Pro\" to accurately reflect the model being used.</edit_summary>\n\t</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t\t<absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n\t\t<lines_viewed>1-2123</lines_viewed>\n\t\t<learnings>This file is the main application component. It handles state management for canvas elements, user interactions, and AI model integration. Key functions like `handleGenerate`, `getAi`, and state variables like `generationModel` and `imageSize` are crucial for the task. The file also contains UI elements for model and image size selection.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_file>\n\t<viewed_file>\n\t\t<absolute_path>/vite.config.ts</absolute_path>\n\t\t<lines_viewed>1-23</lines_viewed>\n\t\t<learnings>This file configures the Vite build tool. It defines how environment variables are exposed to the client-side code, which is important for making the API key available to the `@google/genai` SDK.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_file>\n\t<viewed_file>\n\t\t<absolute_path>/package.json</absolute_path>\n\t\t<lines_viewed>1-23</lines_viewed>\n\t\t<learnings>This file lists project dependencies and scripts. It was reviewed to add a `lint` script, which is necessary for the type-checking step.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_file>\n\t<viewed_file>\n\t\t<absolute_path>/types.ts</absolute_path>\n\t\t<lines_viewed>1-52</lines_viewed>\n\t\t<learnings>This file defines TypeScript interfaces for the application\'s data structures. It was crucial for adding the global declaration of `window.aistudio` to resolve TypeScript errors.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_file>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:handleGenerate</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This function is responsible for initiating AI-powered image generation. It contains logic for selecting the AI model (`generationModel`), checking and setting the API key, and configuring generation parameters like `imageSize`. Modifications here are key to implementing the desired model upgrade and resolution settings.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:generationModel</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This state variable in `App.tsx` controls which AI model (\'flash\' or \'pro\') is used for image generation. It\'s directly related to the user\'s request to switch to a more advanced model.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:imageSize</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This state variable in `App.tsx` determines the desired output resolution for generated images (e.g., \'1K\', \'2K\', \'4K\'). It\'s essential for fulfilling the user\'s requirement for high-quality, 4K images.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>vite.config.ts:define</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This section in `vite.config.ts` exposes environment variables to the client-side code. Specifically, `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` is made available, which is necessary for the `GoogleGenAI` SDK to use the provided API key.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:getAi</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This function is responsible for initializing and returning a `GoogleGenAI` instance. It was modified to ensure a fresh instance is created each time, preventing issues with stale API keys.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>types.ts:declare global</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This section in `types.ts` adds a global declaration for `window.aistudio`, providing type safety for interactions with the AI Studio API and resolving TypeScript errors.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:qualityPro</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This translation key in `App.tsx` was updated to display \"Nano Banana 2\" as the label for the Pro model option.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:usingPro</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This translation key in `App.tsx` was updated to reflect that \"Nano Banana 2\" requires a paid key.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:modelName = \'gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\'</node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This line in `handleGenerate` was initially set to use \'gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\' for the Pro model. It was later corrected to \'gemini-3-pro-image-preview\'.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>\n\t<viewed_code_item>\n\t\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:p className=\"text-[10px] text-blue-500 uppercase tracking-widest font-black\">Ver 3.1 Flash <span className=\"text-gray-300\">| Nano Banana 2</span></p></node_identifier>\n\t\t<learnings>This JSX code snippet in `App.tsx` displays the model version. It was updated to show \"Nano Banana 2\" to align with the UI label changes.</learnings>\n\t</viewed_code_item>"
