  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 3
    user_intent: "AI Model Upgrade and API Key Fixes\n\nThe user\'s primary objective is to resolve persistent \"PERMISSION_DENIED\" errors related to their API key, which are preventing AI model operations. This includes addressing both general permission issues and specific errors indicating a leaked API key. The user also aims to ensure the application correctly prompts for and uses a valid API key when such errors occur, preventing future disruptions."
    session_summary: "## Summary of Conversation and Work Done\n\nThis session focused on upgrading the AI model, enhancing image generation capabilities, and improving API key management and error handling.\n\n### User Goals:\n\n*   Upgrade the AI model to \"Nano Banana 2\" (Gemini 3.1 Flash Image).\n*   Enable high-quality image generation, including 4K resolution and a new 512px option.\n*   Integrate model selection (Flash vs. Pro) and image size options into the application\'s UI and functionality.\n*   Implement robust API key management and error handling, specifically addressing `PERMISSION_DENIED` errors related to invalid or leaked API keys.\n\n### Key Information and Context:\n\n*   **Application Structure:** A React application built with Vite, using the `@google/genai` SDK. It features an infinite canvas for image editing and generation.\n*   **Gemini Models:**\n    *   The \"Pro\" model was upgraded to `gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview` (referred to as \"Nano Banana 2\").\n    *   The \"Flash\" model remains `gemini-2.5-flash-image`.\n*   **Image Generation Configuration:**\n    *   Model selection is handled by the `generationModel` state in `App.tsx`.\n    *   Image size options (\'512\', \'1K\', \'2K\', \'4K\') are managed by the `imageSize` state.\n    *   The `handleGenerate` function in `App.tsx` was updated to correctly pass the selected `imageSize` to the API, with a specific mapping for \'512\' to \'512px\'.\n    *   The `InfiniteCanvas.tsx` component\'s `ImageEditModal` and props were updated to support the new \'512\' resolution option.\n*   **API Key Management and Error Handling:**\n    *   The application uses `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` for the API key, configured via `vite.config.ts`.\n    *   The `handleAiError` function in `App.tsx` was significantly refactored to:\n        *   Catch a broader range of permission-related errors (403, permission denied, leaked key, 404, not found, `API_KEY_INVALID`).\n        *   Provide more informative error messages to the user.\n        *   Consistently prompt the user to select a new API key via `window.aistudio.openSelectKey()` when a permission error occurs.\n        *   Return a boolean indicating whether a new key selection was attempted, allowing for potential retry logic.\n    *   The `getAi` function was refactored to always create a new `GoogleGenAI` instance, ensuring the latest API key is used.\n*   **UI and Translations:**\n    *   UI elements for model selection and image size were updated or added in `App.tsx` and `InfiniteCanvas.tsx`.\n    *   Translations were updated to reflect the new model names and options.\n*   **Build and Linting:**\n    *   A `lint` script (`tsc --noEmit`) was added to `package.json`.\n    *   Build and linting processes were successfully completed after code modifications.\n*   **Dependencies:** `@google/genai`, `react`, `react-dom`.\n*   **Environment Variables:** `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` is crucial for AI functionality.\n*   **Design Decisions:**\n    *   Centralized error handling for AI-related issues in `handleAiError` for consistency.\n    *   Ensured new API instances are created on each call to `getAi` to prevent stale API key issues.\n    *   Added a specific check for `512px` when passing the `imageSize` to the Gemini API.\n\n### Existing Blockers and Bugs:\n\n*   The primary focus was on resolving the `PERMISSION_DENIED` errors related to API keys. The refactored `handleAiError` function aims to address this by prompting the user to re-select their API key.\n\n### Next Steps:\n\n1.  **API Key Testing:** Thoroughly test the API key selection flow after encountering a `PERMISSION_DENIED` error. Ensure the user is prompted correctly and that subsequent API calls succeed with a new key.\n2.  **Model and Resolution Testing:** Verify image generation with all model types (\'flash\', \'pro\') and all resolution options (\'512\', \'1K\', \'2K\', \'4K\') to ensure correct output and functionality.\n3.  **Error Handling Robustness:** Continue to monitor for any other AI-related errors and refine the `handleAiError` function as needed.\n4.  **Code Review:** Conduct a final review of the code for clarity, efficiency, and adherence to best practices."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n<lines_modified>377-390</lines_modified>\n<edit_summary>Improved the `handleAiError` function to more robustly catch and identify permission-related errors (like 403, leaked API key, etc.) and provide a more informative alert to the user, prompting them to select a new API key if `window.aistudio` is available.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n<lines_modified>346-350;804-806</lines_modified>\n<edit_summary>Updated the `imageSize` state to include \'512\' and modified the `handleGenerate` function to correctly map \'512\' to \'512px\' for the API call when the \'pro\' model is selected.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n<target_file>/components/InfiniteCanvas.tsx</target_file>\n<lines_modified>169-173;1008-1015</lines_modified>\n<edit_summary>Updated the `imageSize` type in `InfiniteCanvas.tsx` to include \'512\' and added a corresponding option to the resolution dropdown in the UI.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>350-400</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This section contains the `handleAiError` function, which was modified to better handle permission-denied errors and prompt the user to select a new API key.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>750-850</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This section contains the `handleGenerate` function, where the logic for setting the `imageSize` parameter for the \'pro\' model was updated to accommodate the new \'512\' option.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/vite.config.ts</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1-24</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This file configures Vite and shows how environment variables, specifically `GEMINI_API_KEY`, are loaded and exposed to the client-side as `process.env.API_KEY` and `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`. This is crucial for the application to access the API key.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/components/ImageEditModal.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1-800</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This file contains the `ImageEditModal` component, which includes image editing and generation features. It was reviewed to understand how AI errors are handled within this component, specifically noting the `handleAiError` prop being passed down.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1650-1800</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This section of `App.tsx` contains various event handlers and AI-related functions. The `handleAiError` function is called in several places here, indicating its central role in error management.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_code_item>\n<node_identifier>App.tsx:handleAiError</node_identifier>\n<learnings>This function was refactored to more broadly catch permission-related errors (including \'leaked\' API keys and 404s) and to prompt the user to select a new API key via `window.aistudio.openSelectKey()` if such an error occurs. This directly addresses the user\'s reported errors.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n<node_identifier>App.tsx:handleGenerate</node_identifier>\n<learnings>This function was updated to correctly handle the new \'512\' image size option, mapping it to \'512px\' for the API call. This ensures that the image generation requests with the new resolution are processed correctly.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n<node_identifier>components/InfiniteCanvas.tsx:imageSize</node_identifier>\n<learnings>The type for `imageSize` was updated to include \'512\', and the corresponding UI element (a select dropdown) was modified to offer \'512\' as a resolution option.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n<node_identifier>vite.config.ts:define</node_identifier>\n<learnings>This configuration ensures that the `GEMINI_API_KEY` environment variable is correctly loaded and made available to the client-side code as `process.env.API_KEY` and `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`. This is essential for the application to authenticate with the Google GenAI API.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>"
