  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing API Key Retrieval**\n\nI\'ve realized the `window.aistudio` interface offers limited options: checking for an API key selection and opening the selection interface. This suggests relying on `process.env.API_KEY` for key retrieval. My concern now centers on Vite\'s `define` potentially making the key static, which means a page refresh would be the only recourse for updating the API key.\n\n\n**Refining API Key Retrieval**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a robust key retrieval strategy. I had an idea to avoid static keys by trying a function that checks for the key in multiple ways, but I\'ll stick with the current approach and concentrate on improving error handling. I\'ll add a retry button or more encouraging language to the alert.\n\n\n"
