  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented a robust error handling mechanism to address the **403 Permission Denied** and **Leaked API Key** errors you encountered.\n\n### Changes implemented:\n1.  **Enhanced Error Detection**: Updated the `handleAiError` function to specifically detect 403 errors, permission issues, and leaked key reports. It now correctly parses both string and object-based error messages from the Google GenAI SDK.\n2.  **Automatic Key Selection Prompt**: When a permission or leaked key error is detected, the application will now:\n    *   Display a clear alert explaining the issue.\n    *   Automatically open the **API Key Selection Dialog** (`window.aistudio.openSelectKey()`) to allow you to select a valid paid API key.\n3.  **Dynamic Key Usage**: The `getAi` function has been verified to create a fresh `GoogleGenAI` instance for every request, ensuring that any new API key selected via the dialog is immediately used for the next operation.\n4.  **Comprehensive Coverage**: This error handling is applied across all AI features, including:\n    *   Image Generation (Nano Banana 2 / Gemini 3.1 Flash Image)\n    *   Image Analysis and Style Suggestions\n    *   Prompt Optimization\n    *   Translation Services\n    *   Image Editing and Inpainting (within the Image Edit Modal)\n\n### How to resolve the error:\nWhen you see the \"API Key Permission Error\" alert, simply click \"OK\". The system will open a dialog where you can select a valid API key from a paid Google Cloud project. Once selected, you can retry your generation or analysis, and it should proceed successfully.\n\nThe application is now better equipped to handle API key lifecycle issues and guide you through the resolution process."
    thinking: "**Refining Security Checks**\n\nI\'ve got the linting passed, which is a good start. Now, I\'m diving deeper into the security aspect for `gemini-3-flash-preview` usage. I\'m considering integrating `window.aistudio.hasSelectedApiKey()` into `handleAnalyzeElement` and other locations where it\'s used. Making sure this safeguard is implemented correctly will be essential.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have implemented a robust error handling mechanism to address the **403 Permission Denied** and **Leaked API Key** errors you encountered.\n\n### Changes implemented:\n1.  **Enhanced Error Detection**: Updated the `handleAiError` function to specifically detect 403 errors, permission issues, and leaked key reports. It now correctly parses both string and object-based error messages from the Google GenAI SDK.\n2.  **Automatic Key Selection Prompt**: When a permission or leaked key error is detected, the application will now:\n    *   Display a clear alert explaining the issue.\n    *   Automatically open the **API Key Selection Dialog** (`window.aistudio.openSelectKey()`) to allow you to select a valid paid API key.\n3.  **Dynamic Key Usage**: The `getAi` function has been verified to create a fresh `GoogleGenAI` instance for every request, ensuring that any new API key selected via the dialog is immediately used for the next operation.\n4.  **Comprehensive Coverage**: This error handling is applied across all AI features, including:\n    *   Image Generation (Nano Banana 2 / Gemini 3.1 Flash Image)\n    *   Image Analysis and Style Suggestions\n    *   Prompt Optimization\n    *   Translation Services\n    *   Image Editing and Inpainting (within the Image Edit Modal)\n\n### How to resolve the error:\nWhen you see the \"API Key Permission Error\" alert, simply click \"OK\". The system will open a dialog where you can select a valid API key from a paid Google Cloud project. Once selected, you can retry your generation or analysis, and it should proceed successfully.\n\nThe application is now better equipped to handle API key lifecycle issues and guide you through the resolution process."
